# The ignore file for `Containerfile.freebsd.proxy`.  Passed explicitly, for
# the reason its two siblings give: buildah has no
# `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` lookup, and a root-level `.containerignore` would
# satisfy the letter of the "no container file at the repository root" guard in
# `usage/tests/test_all.py` while defeating it.
#
#   buildah bud --ignorefile server/oci/Containerfile.freebsd.proxy.containerignore ...
#
# WHAT IS NOT IN THIS CONTEXT, AND WHY THAT IS THE POINT
#
#   `server/srv/` in its entirety.  This image proxies bytes: it parses no
#   record, holds no token, opens no store and has no interpreter to do any of
#   it with.  Leaving the package out of the CONTEXT rather than merely out of
#   the COPY list means a later edit cannot put it back without also editing
#   this file, which is a decision somebody has to make on purpose.
#
# The context is the REPOSITORY ROOT, because the image needs `LICENCE`, the
# configuration under `server/oci/nginx/` and the staged FreeBSD tree, and no
# one of them is a parent of the others.
*
!/LICENCE
!/server/oci/nginx/**
!/server/oci/entrypoint-proxy.sh
!/server/oci/stage-freebsd-proxy/**
**/__pycache__
